HeaderInclude
config/jrisc/jrisc-opts.h

mcpu=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(jrisc_cpu) Var(jrisc_cpu) Init(JRISC_CPU_GPU)
-mcpu=CPU	Generate code for the TOM GPU (tom, gpu) or the JERRY DSP (jerry, dsp).

Enum
Name(jrisc_cpu) Type(enum jrisc_cpu_type)
Known Jaguar RISC processors (for use with the -mcpu= option):

EnumValue
Enum(jrisc_cpu) String(gpu) Value(JRISC_CPU_GPU)

EnumValue
Enum(jrisc_cpu) String(tom) Value(JRISC_CPU_GPU)

EnumValue
Enum(jrisc_cpu) String(dsp) Value(JRISC_CPU_DSP)

EnumValue
Enum(jrisc_cpu) String(jerry) Value(JRISC_CPU_DSP)

mgpu
Target RejectNegative Alias(mcpu=, gpu)
Generate code for the TOM GPU.

mdsp
Target RejectNegative Alias(mcpu=, dsp)
Generate code for the JERRY DSP.

mjaguar-object
Target RejectNegative
Link the program as a 68000 object, to be linked with the 68000 code of a Jaguar program.

mfix-hazards
Target Var(jrisc_fix_hazards) Init(1)
Wait for a pending divide or load from main RAM before an instruction that the pipeline does not make wait for it (TOM bugs 2, 13 and 25).

mfix-dsp-stores
Target Var(jrisc_fix_dsp_stores) Init(-1)
Work around the DSP bug that corrupts a store to main RAM not preceded by a completed load from it (on by default for the DSP).

mlocal-frame-limit=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(jrisc_local_frame_limit) Init(64)
-mlocal-frame-limit=N	Keep locals of up to N bytes on the stack in local RAM; put larger ones in main RAM.
